{"book":21,"chapter":12,"context":{"chapter":12,"title":"Remember Your Creator","summary":"A haunting poem pictures old age and death as a house falling silent, urging the young to remember their Creator early. The book closes by describing the Preacher's work and giving its conclusion: fear God and keep His commandments.","background":"Many read vv. 3–5 as a picture of the aging body: trembling 'keepers' (arms), bent 'strong men' (legs), few 'grinders' (teeth), darkened 'windows' (eyes), and almond blossoms (white hair). Other readings exist, and the details are debated. Verse 7 reverses Genesis 2:7: dust returns to the earth, and the spirit to God.","customs":[{"term":"The silver cord… the golden bowl","verses":"12:6","note":"Probably a lamp bowl hanging from a cord. When the cord snaps, the lamp shatters and the light goes out."},{"term":"Goads","verses":"12:11","note":"Pointed sticks used to drive oxen forward. Wise words prod and steer."}],"watchFor":["The book ends with the cry it began with (v. 8; 1:2).","In vv. 9–14 a different voice speaks about the Preacher.","The final word is God's judgment of every secret thing (v. 14)."],"connections":["Genesis 2:7","Genesis 3:19","Acts 26:14","2 Corinthians 5:10"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וּזְכֹר","uzekhor","H2142","HC/Vqv2ms","and remember"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["בּוֹרְאֶיךָ","bor'eikha","H1254","HVqrmsc/Sp2ms","creator<s> your"],["בִּימֵי","bimei","H3117","HR/Ncmpc","in [the] days of"],["בְּחוּרֹתֶיךָ","bechuroteikha","H979","HNcfpc/Sp2ms","youth<s> your"],["עַד","'ad","H5704","HR","until"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","that"],["לֹא","lo'-","H3808","HTn","not"],["יָבֹאוּ","yavo'u","H935","HVqi3mp","they will come"],["יְמֵי","yemei","H3117","HNcmpc","[the] days of"],["הָרָעָה","hara'ah","H7451","HTd/Ncfsa","<the> evil"],["וְהִגִּיעוּ","vehigi'u","H5060","Hc/Vhq3cp","and they will arrive"],["שָׁנִים","shanim","H8141","HNcmpa","years"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["תֹּאמַר","tomar","H559"